"SDD maturity  0/100 · Vibe coding   Verification-tax reduction  −0%   Harness readiness  0/100    Ad-hoc prompting; the spec lives in people’s heads; code is the only artifact.  Reference 2.1: Spec-Driven Development makes the spec the primary executable artifact. Higher SDD maturity cuts the verification tax (up to −50% at 100) and mitigates the AI code-quality premium (EV-23). Harness readiness (AGENTS.md, GUARDRAILS.md, skills, hooks, MCP) is the tooling foundation. CC-SDD-01.    | Y1 coaching load  40%  ≈ €558K/yr   Y2 coaching load  30%  ≈ €419K/yr   Y3 coaching load  20%  ≈ €279K/yr    Autonomy tier  Phase  Mechanism    Intensive coaching  Y1  Preceptor 3:1–5:1, review-first, explain-the-code gates   On-demand support  Y1–Y2  Office hours, pairing on demand, champions relay   Self-service  Y2–Y3  Playbooks, internal certification, communities of practice   Community of practice  cruise  Peer support only; coaching decays deliberately     Reference 3.2/4.2: coaching starts at ~40% of capacity and decays to ~20% at cruise as support is weaned (intensive → on-demand → self-service → community). Costs are indicative (analytical) and overlap the HRI change model. CC-COACH-01.    | Reference 3.3/6.3: DORA alone is no longer enough at L4. Steer four families together; measure before committing (T0/T1/T2), and move beyond billable-staffing rate as the sole performance metric.  DORA — flow & stability  Deploy frequency  target ↑  higher with agentic CI/CD; watch it does not trade off stability   Lead time for change  target ↓  shorter as coding ceases to be the bottleneck   Change failure rate  guardrail  stability guardrail — +25% AI adoption came with −7.2% stability (DORA 2024)   MTTR  target ↓  faster recovery with agent-assisted triage      SPACE — beyond throughput  Satisfaction & well-being  survey  developer experience under human+agent delivery   Performance (outcomes)  outcome  value delivered, not lines produced   Activity  context  use with care — volume can inflate   Communication & collaboration  flow  pod & review-gate health      AI signals  AI-code share  context  % of merged code with agent authorship   Cost per successful result  $/result  total cost / accepted output — see FinOps   AI-attributed defect rate  guardrail  tie to the AI code-quality premium (EV-23)   Verification tax  %  review effort turning addressable into net gain (EV-27)    PR cycle time by AI involvement  split  segment flow by agent involvement      Human early-warning indicators  Time-to-judgment  ↓ risk if rising  how long to reach a sound decision — erosion signal   Bus factor  ↑ better  concentration of irreplaceable knowledge   % mentoring compensated  target ≥ 100%  is coaching time protected vs billable pressure · HRI 50/100      The socle is analytical (target bands & guardrails). Values feed from the model where available (verification tax, HRI); the rest are steering targets. CC-SOCLE-01.    | Gate / artifact  Definition    Non-bypassable CI gates  Mandatory before merge; the wall that does not move   C2 quality control  Tests, mutation testing, security scanning   Human-in-the-Lead review  Risk-based review effort by phase (see supervision matrix)   Anti-false-success guardrails  Detect deleted tests, disabled lint, lowered coverage   Enlarged Definition of Done  Adds: agent provenance recorded, review evidence, security check, doc updated, AI-BOM entry   AI-BOM (AI Bill of Materials)  Models, datasets, MCP services, skills used — traceability & supply-chain audit     Reference 5.1: the CI is the wall that does not move. These gates are mandatory and non-bypassable before merge; the enlarged DoD and the AI-BOM are exported in the Critical & Regulated report (EV-11). CC-GATE-01.   "